.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt OTEL.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm otel.conf
.Nd system OpenTelemetry configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/otel.conf
.Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
configures how base system programs export telemetry with the
OpenTelemetry protocol (OTLP).
The base system contains no collector or agent: the programs export
directly to the receiver named here.
It is read through one configuration path of the base exporter library
.Pq Xr oe_config_load 3
by every program exporting with OTLP:
.Xr dtrace 1
.Pq Fl x Cm otel=otlp ,
.Xr bsdinstruments 8
.Pq Fl -format Cm otel ,
.Xr hwstat 8 ,
.Xr otelpfd 8
and
.Xr otelauditd 8 ,
and by
.Xr otelconf 8 ,
which validates it.
.Pp
Settings are resolved per key, highest precedence first:
.Bl -enum -offset indent -compact
.It
the program's command line;
.It
the standard
.Ev OTEL_*
environment variables, a signal's own variable
.Pq Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT
before the general one
.Pq Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT ;
.It
.Pa /etc/otel.conf ,
a signal block's key before the general key;
.It
.Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf ;
.It
built-in defaults.
.El
.Pp
.Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf
is replaced on upgrade and must not be edited.
Put local settings in
.Pa /etc/otel.conf ;
a key set there replaces the default, and a key of an object
.Pq for example one resource attribute
replaces just that key.
.Pp
Both files use UCL syntax
.Pq see Xr libucl 3
restricted to plain values: macros such as
.Ic .include
and file variables are not processed.
Unknown keys, wrongly typed values and duplicated keys are errors,
so a misspelled key never silently falls back to its default.
.Pp
Starting the out-of-the-box telemetry services is controlled by
.Va otel_enable
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 ;
see
.Sx SERVICES .
.Sh EXPORTER KEYS
.Bl -tag -width "host_id_file"
.It Ic enable Pq boolean, default Dv true
Apply this configuration.
When false, programs ignore the file
.Pq as if it did not exist
and the rc.d OpenTelemetry services refuse to start.
.It Ic export Pq object
Where telemetry goes:
.Bl -tag -width "directory"
.It Ic target Pq string, default Qq otlp
.Qq otlp
sends OTLP to
.Ic endpoint
with
.Ic protocol .
.Qq file
writes OTLP JSON Lines instead: one
.Li ExportLogsServiceRequest ,
.Li ExportMetricsServiceRequest
or
.Li ExportTraceServiceRequest
object per line, the format of the OpenTelemetry Collector's file
exporter, which its
.Li otlpjsonfile
receiver reads back.
Each program writes its own file,
.Pa <directory>/<program>.jsonl
.Po
.Pa dtrace.jsonl
for
.Xr dtrace 1
.Fl x Cm otel=otlp ,
.Pa bsdinstruments.jsonl
for
.Xr bsdinstruments 8
.Fl -format Cm otel
and the
.Pa otel_dtrace
service,
.Pa hwstat.jsonl ,
.Pa otelpfd.jsonl ,
.Pa otelauditd.jsonl
.Pc ,
created with mode 0640 and synchronized to disk at least once a second
while records arrive.
An endpoint from the command line,
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
or a signal's
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ Ns Ar SIGNAL Ns Ev _ENDPOINT
still selects OTLP export for that program; the endpoints of the signal
blocks are not used, and the spool is not used, with the file target.
Profiles
.Pq experimental
are written as whole
.Li ExportProfilesServiceRequest
lines, whose JSON form is at Development maturity in opentelemetry-proto
1.10 and may change with it.
A file target that cannot be opened is an error, not a fallback.
.Pp
.Xr newsyslog 8
rotates the files
.Pq Pa /etc/newsyslog.conf.d/otel.conf ,
and the writers cooperate without losing or splitting a record: the
services and
.Xr bsdinstruments 8
reopen their file on
.Dv SIGHUP ,
which newsyslog sends to the process named by
.Pa /var/run/otel/<service>.child.pid
before it compresses the rotated file; every writer, including
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
also notices within a second that the path names a new file and
reopens it.
.It Ic directory Pq path, default Pa /var/log/otel
Directory of the files, owned by
.Ql _otel
with mode 0750; the rc.d services create it when missing.
.El
.It Ic endpoint Pq string, default Qq
Base URL of the OTLP receiver, for example an OpenTelemetry Collector.
With the OTLP/HTTP protocols, signals are sent to
.Pa /v1/metrics ,
.Pa /v1/logs
and
.Pa /v1/traces
below it; with
.Qq grpc
it names the OTLP/gRPC server.
.Pp
Not used with the
.Ic export.target
.Qq file .
.Pp
The default is empty: nothing in the base system listens for OTLP, so
the configuration names no receiver until one is set.
The rc.d services
.Pq Sx SERVICES ,
.Xr otelpfd 8
and
.Xr otelauditd 8
refuse to start without an export target, an endpoint or the file
target
.Po
.Ql otelconf check -t
fails
.Pc .
A program a user runs and asks for OTLP explicitly
.Po
.Xr dtrace 1
.Fl x Cm otel=otlp ,
.Xr bsdinstruments 8
and
.Xr hwstat 8
.Fl -format Cm otel
.Pc
then uses the conventional default of the OpenTelemetry
specification,
.Qq http://localhost:4318 ,
or
.Qq http://localhost:4317
when the protocol is
.Qq grpc ,
where a collector the user runs listens by default.
.It Ic protocol Pq string, default Qq http/protobuf
OTLP protocol of the tools and services:
.Qq http/protobuf
.Pq OTLP/HTTP, protobuf bodies ,
.Qq grpc
.Pq OTLP/gRPC
or
.Qq http/json
.Pq OTLP/HTTP, JSON bodies .
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL
and the tools' command line options take precedence.
With
.Qq grpc ,
.Ic endpoint
must name an OTLP/gRPC receiver, normally on port 4317.
The protocol applies only to
.Ic export.target
.Qq otlp :
the
.Qq file
target always writes OTLP JSON Lines, whatever the protocol.
.It Ic compression Pq string, default Qq gzip
.Qq gzip
or
.Qq none .
.It Ic timeout_ms Pq integer, default 10000
Per-request timeout in milliseconds, 1 to 600000.
.It Ic headers_file Pq path, default Qq
File of extra HTTP headers, typically credentials, for
.Ic endpoint ;
see
.Sx CREDENTIALS FILES .
The headers are sent only when the resolved endpoint is
.Ic endpoint
itself, never to an endpoint given on the command line or in
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT .
.It Ic host_id_file Pq path, default Pa /etc/hostid
File holding the host UUID, written at boot by the
.Pa hostid
rc.d script.
Its first line becomes the
.Va host.id
resource attribute unless
.Ic resource
sets it.
A missing file is ignored; a file without a UUID is an error.
.Qq
disables the lookup.
.It Ic resource Pq object
Resource attributes attached to every record, as quoted names and
string values.
Names consist of letters, digits and
.Ql .\& ,
.Ql _ ,
.Ql - ,
.Ql / .
An empty value removes an attribute set by the defaults file.
The defaults set
.Va service.namespace
to
.Qq 5bsd
and
.Va deployment.environment.name
to
.Qq production .
At most 32 attributes are accepted.
.It Ic logs , metrics , traces , profiles Pq object
Settings of one signal, overriding the general keys for it, so each
signal may use its own collector and transport:
.Bl -tag -width "headers_file"
.It Ic endpoint Pq string
The signal's full URL, used as-is: OTLP/HTTP requests of the signal go
to its path exactly, with nothing appended
.Pq OTLP/gRPC uses its host and port .
.It Ic protocol Pq string
As the general key.
Profiles are sent with
.Qq http/protobuf
or
.Qq grpc
only.
.It Ic compression Pq string
As the general key.
.It Ic timeout_ms Pq integer
1 to 600000.
.It Ic headers_file Pq path
A credentials file, with the same checks as the general one, whose
headers are sent only to this block's
.Ic endpoint .
A block with an
.Ic endpoint
but no
.Ic headers_file
sends the general file's headers to it.
.El
.Pp
A key the block does not set comes from the general keys; an
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ Ns Ar SIGNAL Ns Ev _ Ns Ar SETTING
or general
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ Ns Ar SETTING
variable, or the command line, overrides the block's setting, and the
general file's headers go only to the general
.Ic endpoint
and to the endpoints of blocks without a
.Ic headers_file
of their own.
.It Ic spool Pq object
Persistent buffering of OTLP batches the collector could not take
.Pq the Qq otlp target only :
.Bl -tag -width "max_bytes"
.It Ic directory Pq path, default Pa /var/spool/otel
Every program exporting with OTLP
.Po
.Xr dtrace 1
.Fl x Cm otel=otlp ,
.Xr bsdinstruments 8
.Fl -format Cm otel ,
.Xr hwstat 8 ,
.Xr otelpfd 8 ,
.Xr otelauditd 8
.Pc
that is not given a spool on its command line spools to
.Pa <directory>/<program>.spool
when it may write this directory (the services, which run as root or
switch to
.Ql _otel ,
and root may; other users export without a spool).
Each spool file has one owner at a time, held with a lock on
.Pa <program>.spool.lock ;
a second instance of the same program exports without a spool.
.It Ic max_bytes Pq integer, default 268435456
Bound on buffered data, 1 MiB to 1 TiB, applied to each spool file and
to a command-line spool given without its own bound; batches beyond it
are dropped and counted.
UCL size suffixes such as
.Qq 256mb
are accepted.
.El
.El
.Sh CREDENTIALS FILES
A credentials file holds one header per line as
.Dl Name: value
Blank lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
are ignored.
Names must be HTTP tokens; values must not contain control characters
other than tab.
.Dv Content-Type ,
.Dv Content-Length ,
.Dv Content-Encoding ,
.Dv Host
and
.Dv Connection
are set by the exporter and are refused.
.Pp
The file must be a regular file
.Pq not a symbolic link
owned by root or by the reading user, with no group or other
permission bits: mode 0600 or 0400.
A file that violates this, or that is configured but missing, makes the
whole configuration fail to load, so telemetry is never sent without
the configured credentials.
.Sh FILE CHECKS
Both configuration files must be regular files, not symbolic links,
owned by root or the reading user, not writable by group or others,
at most 64 KiB, and free of NUL bytes.
A missing file is not an error.
A credentials file is limited to 16 KiB and 32 headers.
.Sh SERVICES
The following
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables start the telemetry services; all default to off.
.Bl -tag -width "otel_auditd_enable"
.It Va otel_enable
Master switch.
Each service variable below that is left empty follows it.
The services need an export target
.Po
.Ic endpoint
or
.Ic export.target
.Qq file
.Pc ,
or
.Va otel_endpoint
in
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.It Va otel_hwstat_enable
.Xr hwstat 8
hardware metrics.
.It Va otelpfd_enable
.Xr pf 4
statistics,
.Xr otelpfd 8 .
.It Va otelauditd_enable
Audit records as log records,
.Xr otelauditd 8 .
.It Va otel_dtrace_enable
DTrace-derived system metrics via
.Xr bsdinstruments 8 .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "OTELCONF_DEFAULTS"
.It Ev OTELCONF_FILE , Ev OTELCONF_DEFAULTS
Read these files instead of
.Pa /etc/otel.conf
and
.Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf ,
for trying a configuration or testing.
Ignored by set-user-ID and set-group-ID programs.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/defaults/otel.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/otel.conf
local settings
.It Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf
default settings
.It Pa /etc/hostid
host UUID
.It Pa /var/spool/otel
spool directory
.It Pa /var/log/otel
file target directory
.It Pa /etc/newsyslog.conf.d/otel.conf
rotation of the file target
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Export everything to a remote collector with a bearer token:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /etc/otel.conf
endpoint = "https://collector.example.org:4318";
headers_file = "/etc/otel/collector.headers";
.Ed
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# install -m 0600 /dev/null /etc/otel/collector.headers
# echo 'Authorization: Bearer TOKEN' > /etc/otel/collector.headers
# otelconf check -t
# sysrc otel_enable=YES
.Ed
.Pp
Send traces to a separate collector over OTLP/gRPC with their own
token, and the other signals to the general endpoint:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /etc/otel.conf
endpoint = "https://collector.example.org:4318";
headers_file = "/etc/otel/collector.headers";
traces {
	endpoint = "https://traces.example.org:4317";
	protocol = "grpc";
	headers_file = "/etc/otel/traces.headers";
}
profiles { protocol = "http/protobuf"; }
.Ed
.Pp
Keep everything in local files, without a collector:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /etc/otel.conf
export { target = "file"; }
.Ed
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# sysrc otel_enable=YES
# service otelpfd start
# tail -1 /var/log/otel/otelpfd.jsonl
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
.Xr libotelexport 3 ,
.Xr libucl 3 ,
.Xr oe_sysconf 3 ,
.Xr newsyslog.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr bsdinstruments 8 ,
.Xr hwstat 8 ,
.Xr otelauditd 8 ,
.Xr otelconf 8 ,
